{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c7d9e5b0-2222-4333-8444-555566667777",
    "name": "auth-server FULL (features 1-14)",
    "description": "Consolidated Postman collection for every feature shipped on the auth-server.\n\nOrganized by feature. Each folder contains the requests + a description of what to observe.\n\nDefaults:\n  base_url         http://localhost:8095\n  zipkin_url       http://localhost:9411\n  vault_url        http://localhost:8200\n  admin_user       admin\n  admin_pass       password\n  m2m_client_id    m2m-client\n  m2m_client_sec   m2m-secret\n  demo_client_id   demo-client\n  demo_client_sec  secret\n  registrar_id     registrar\n  registrar_sec    registrar-secret\n  api_admin_id     api-admin\n  api_admin_sec    api-admin-secret\n\nAuto-cached tokens:\n  admin_token           (JWT for API mirror — cached by pre-request scripts)\n  registrar_token       (JWT for DCR endpoint)\n\nRun order recommendation:\n  1. Setup → Discovery + JWKS  (see the server is up)\n  2. OAuth2 core → m2m token   (populates access_token)\n  3. Any feature folder in any order — token caching handles auth.\n\nBrowser-only sections (marked with *) need a real browser + interactive login:\n  - Feature 8 Consent screen\n  - Feature 5 Account lockout via login form",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup — Discovery + Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /.well-known/openid-configuration",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/.well-known/openid-configuration",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": [".well-known", "openid-configuration"]
            },
            "description": "OIDC discovery document — proves the auth-server is reachable and returns metadata (token endpoint, JWKS URL, supported grants)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /oauth2/jwks",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('has at least 1 key', () => pm.expect(body.keys.length).to.be.greaterThan(0));",
                  "const kid = body.keys[0].kid;",
                  "console.log('primary kid:', kid);",
                  "// Feature 11 marker — kid starts with 'vault:' when Vault backend is active",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('current_kid', kid);",
                  "if (kid.startsWith('vault:')) {",
                  "  console.log('Feature 11: Vault backend active');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/oauth2/jwks",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "jwks"]
            },
            "description": "Public keys for JWT signature verification. Feature 3 adds SECONDARY keys after rotation (multiple entries); Feature 11 (Vault backend) prefixes the kid with 'vault:auth-server:v'."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /actuator/health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/actuator/health",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["actuator", "health"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. OAuth2 core (token endpoints)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /oauth2/token — m2m (client_credentials)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (b.access_token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('m2m_token', b.access_token);",
                  "  console.log('m2m_token cached');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('has access_token', () => pm.expect(b).to.have.property('access_token'));",
                  "",
                  "// Decode + show custom claims (Feature 7)",
                  "const payload = JSON.parse(atob(b.access_token.split('.')[1].replace(/-/g,'+').replace(/_/g,'/')));",
                  "console.log('JWT payload:', payload);",
                  "pm.test('Feature 7: subject_type=client claim present', () => pm.expect(payload.subject_type).to.equal('client'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{m2m_client_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{m2m_client_sec}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "client_credentials", "type": "text" },
                { "key": "scope", "value": "read", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/oauth2/token",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "token"]
            },
            "description": "Machine-to-machine token. Test script:\n  - Caches m2m_token variable\n  - Decodes JWT payload and asserts Feature 7's subject_type=client claim"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /oauth2/introspect",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{m2m_client_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{m2m_client_sec}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "token", "value": "{{m2m_token}}", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/oauth2/token/../oauth2/introspect",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "token", "..", "oauth2", "introspect"]
            },
            "description": "Verifies the token's signature and returns claims. On Feature 11 (Vault backend) this proves the round-trip: Vault signed → Nimbus verified using Vault's public JWKS."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /oauth2/revoke",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{m2m_client_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{m2m_client_sec}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "token", "value": "{{m2m_token}}", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/oauth2/revoke",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "revoke"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "12. Dynamic Client Registration (RFC 7591)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Step 1 — bootstrap: registrar token (scope=client.create)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('registrar_token', b.access_token);",
                  "pm.test('has client.create scope', () => pm.expect(b.scope).to.include('client.create'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{registrar_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{registrar_sec}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "client_credentials", "type": "text" },
                { "key": "scope", "value": "client.create", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/oauth2/token",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "token"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Step 2 — POST /connect/register (create dcr-test-app)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('201 created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('client_id returned', () => pm.expect(b).to.have.property('client_id'));",
                  "pm.test('plaintext client_secret returned ONCE', () => pm.expect(b).to.have.property('client_secret'));",
                  "pm.test('registration_access_token returned', () => pm.expect(b).to.have.property('registration_access_token'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('dcr_client_id', b.client_id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('dcr_reg_token', b.registration_access_token);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{registrar_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"client_name\": \"dcr-test-app\",\n  \"redirect_uris\": [\"https://myapp.example.com/callback\"],\n  \"grant_types\": [\"authorization_code\", \"refresh_token\"],\n  \"response_types\": [\"code\"],\n  \"scope\": \"openid profile\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/connect/register",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["connect", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Feature 12: RFC 7591 dynamic client registration. Test script asserts 201 + presence of client_id/client_secret/registration_access_token, and caches them."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Step 3 — RFC 7592 read (verify)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{dcr_reg_token}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/connect/register?client_id={{dcr_client_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["connect", "register"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "client_id", "value": "{{dcr_client_id}}" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Uses the registration_access_token from step 2. Returns client metadata (secret now BCrypt-hashed, no plaintext)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "14. REST API mirror",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Step 1 — bootstrap: admin token (admin.read + admin.write)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('admin_token', b.access_token);",
                  "pm.test('has admin.write', () => pm.expect(b.scope).to.include('admin.write'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{api_admin_id}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{api_admin_sec}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "client_credentials", "type": "text" },
                { "key": "scope", "value": "admin.read admin.write admin.unlock", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/oauth2/token",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "token"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /api/v1/admin/clients",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/admin/clients",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "clients"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /api/v1/admin/clients (create rest-test)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('rest_test_id', b.id);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"clientId\": \"rest-test\",\n  \"clientName\": \"REST Test\",\n  \"clientSecret\": \"restsec\",\n  \"grantTypes\": [\"client_credentials\"],\n  \"authMethods\": [\"client_secret_basic\"],\n  \"scopes\": [\"read\"]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/admin/clients",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "clients"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /api/v1/admin/clients/{id}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/admin/clients/{{rest_test_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "clients", "{{rest_test_id}}"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "DELETE /api/v1/admin/clients/{id}",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('204 no content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/admin/clients/{{rest_test_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "clients", "{{rest_test_id}}"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /api/v1/admin/users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/admin/users",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "users"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /api/v1/admin/audit",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{admin_token}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/admin/audit?page=0",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "audit"],
              "query": [{ "key": "page", "value": "0" }]
            },
            "description": "Feature 4: audit log paginated. Every CRUD action from browser or REST leaves a row here. `actor` field: 'admin' = browser session, 'api-admin' = this JWT."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "NEGATIVE — 401 without token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/admin/clients",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "clients"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "NEGATIVE — 403 wrong scope (get read-only token, try POST)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Fetch a token with ONLY admin.read; the POST should 403.",
                  "pm.sendRequest({",
                  "  url: pm.collectionVariables.get('base_url') + '/oauth2/token',",
                  "  method: 'POST',",
                  "  header: {",
                  "    'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded',",
                  "    'Authorization': 'Basic ' + btoa(pm.collectionVariables.get('api_admin_id') + ':' + pm.collectionVariables.get('api_admin_sec'))",
                  "  },",
                  "  body: { mode:'urlencoded', urlencoded: [",
                  "    {key:'grant_type', value:'client_credentials'},",
                  "    {key:'scope', value:'admin.read'}",
                  "  ]}",
                  "}, (err, res) => {",
                  "  if (!err && res.code === 200) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('read_only_token', res.json().access_token);",
                  "  }",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('RFC 7807 body', () => pm.response.to.be.header('Content-Type', 'application/problem+json'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{read_only_token}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"clientId\": \"scope-test\",\n  \"clientName\": \"x\",\n  \"clientSecret\": \"y\",\n  \"grantTypes\": [\"client_credentials\"],\n  \"authMethods\": [\"client_secret_basic\"],\n  \"scopes\": [\"read\"]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/admin/clients",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "admin", "clients"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
