        {
          "name": "* Feature 8 — Consent screen",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/oauth2/authorize?response_type=code&client_id={{demo_client_id}}&redirect_uri=http://127.0.0.1:8097/login/oauth2/code/demo-client&scope=openid+profile+read&state=xyz",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth2", "authorize"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "response_type", "value": "code" },
                { "key": "client_id", "value": "{{demo_client_id}}" },
                { "key": "redirect_uri", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8097/login/oauth2/code/demo-client" },
                { "key": "scope", "value": "openid+profile+read" },
                { "key": "state", "value": "xyz" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Open this URL in a browser, not Postman. Login as admin/password → land on our Bootstrap-styled consent page (Feature 8). Uncheck 'read', click Approve → redirect to 127.0.0.1:8097 with ?code=... (browser will 404 — that's expected, no client app running there).\n\nPRE-REQ: demo-client must have requireAuthorizationConsent=true. Set it via /admin/clients edit form OR via /api/v1/admin/clients PUT."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "* Feature 5 — Account lockout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "some-user", "type": "text" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "WRONG", "type": "text" }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/login",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["login"]
            },
            "description": "Feature 5 requires 5 sequential failed logins to lock a user. Postman + CSRF is awkward. Recommend the shell for this:\n\n```bash\nCJAR=/tmp/lockout.txt\nfor i in 1 2 3 4 5; do\n  rm -f $CJAR\n  CSRF=$(curl -s -c $CJAR http://localhost:8095/login \\\n    | grep -oE 'name=\"_csrf\"[^>]*value=\"[^\"]+\"' | head -1 \\\n    | sed 's/.*value=\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/')\n  curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" -c $CJAR -b $CJAR \\\n    --data-urlencode \"username=locktest\" \\\n    --data-urlencode \"password=WRONG\" \\\n    --data-urlencode \"_csrf=$CSRF\" \\\n    http://localhost:8095/login\ndone\n```\n\nThen unlock via the REST endpoint in folder '5. Account lockout — unlock via REST'."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
